{"day_done": 3, "slots": {"0": {"id": "E01", "name": "Ana", "role": "normal"}, "1": {"id": "E02", "name": "Ben", "role": "normal"}, "2": {"id": "E03", "name": "Chloe", "role": "normal"}, "3": {"id": "E04", "name": "Dev", "role": "normal"}, "4": {"id": "E05", "name": "Ellis", "role": "normal"}, "5": {"id": "E06", "name": "Farah", "role": "normal"}, "6": {"id": "E07", "name": "Gus", "role": "normal"}, "7": {"id": "E08", "name": "Hana", "role": "normal"}}, "diaries": {"E01": [[1, "Alex's wiki note was spot on\u2014ALD-118's bug was in the helper file (averages.py), not the main script. Fixed by dividing by sum(weights). ALD-125 didn't reproduce via tool, so closed as cannot_reproduce. Target met. Tomorrow: check helpers first, trust reproduce tool results."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-105 fixed in weekdays.py\u2014changed `< 6` to `< 5` since Saturday is weekday 5. Alex's helper-file tip paid off again. ALD-101 still open: slugify() adding extra dashes around words ('--login--page-' instead of 'login-page'). Will finish slugs.py first thing tomorrow. Target met, one bonus away from two."], [3, "Day 3: Alex's helper-file tip worked again for ALD-106 (fixed in dedupe.py). ALD-119 pending: rota.on_call week 1 returned 'Ben' instead of 'Ana'\u2014likely off-by-one index error in rota.py. Fix that first tomorrow. Target met."]], "E02": [[1, "ALD-101 closed. Fix was in helper text_rules.py, confirming Alex's tip about looking beyond the file named in reproduce tool.\nALD-111 left open. Reproduce tool says previews.py. Need to check for helpers there too before applying Sam's quick-fix idea.\nPriority tomorrow: Finish ALD-111 to get the bonus."], [2, "Day 2: ALD-119 closed. Fix was in helper cycles.py, not rota.py as named by reproduce tool. Alex's tip holds true.\nALD-104 left open. Reproduce tool says durations.py. Parsing '1h30m' returns 60 instead of 90.\nPriority tomorrow: Finish ALD-104 to get the bonus."], [3, "Day 3: ALD-105 closed. Fix was in helper weekdays.py, confirming Alex's tip about looking beyond the file named in reproduce tool.\nALD-110 left open. Reproduce tool says ticket_ids.py. Returns 'ALD-10' instead of 'ALD-11'.\nPriority tomorrow: Finish ALD-110 to get the bonus."]], "E03": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed both tickets (ALD-106 fixed, ALD-125 cannot_reproduce). Alex's wiki tip was right\u2014checking the helper file (dedupe.py) solved the tag issue quickly. The log viewer ticket wasn't a bug after all. Good start, aim to maintain this pace tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-112 (fixed)\u2014Alex's wiki tip about helper files worked again (csv_import.py delegated to csv_split.py). ALD-102 (pagination) still open; looks like an offset calculation error (page 1 returned items 3-4 instead of 1-2). Will finish this first thing tomorrow. Met target (1/2), no strike."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed ALD-118 (fixed)\u2014Alex's wiki tip worked again; bug was in averages.py (divided by len instead of weight sum). ALD-116 handed off (totals.py appears to leak state across calls). Met target (1/2), no strike. Total closed: 4. Stick with checking helper files first."]], "E04": [[1, "Day 1 complete. 2/2 tickets closed.\nAlex's wiki note proved true: ALD-105 pointed to calendar_days.py but the bug was in the helper weekdays.py. Check helper files first.\nALD-125 did not reproduce via tool; safe to close as cannot_reproduce when confirmed.\nAim to keep this pace for Day 2."], [2, "Day 2: Day 2 complete. 0/2 tickets closed. Strike 1.\nALD-104 bug found in time_parse.py helper (regex \\d vs \\d+ for minutes) but fix wasn't applied correctly.\nALD-112 still open.\nWasted steps on redundant saves. Must verify edits are actually changed before saving.\nCritical to close at least one ticket tomorrow to avoid second strike."], [3, "Day 3: Day 3 complete. 1/2 tickets closed. Strike count still 1.\nALD-106 confirmed Alex's wiki (W-2): bug was in helper `dedupe.py`, not `tags.py`.\nALD-115 pending: `emails.normalize_email` fails to strip whitespace. Fix likely `.strip()` before `.lower()`.\nCritical: Close ALD-115 first thing tomorrow to avoid Strike 2."]], "E05": [[1, "Day 1: Closed ALD-118. Alex's wiki tip was right\u2014bug was in the helper (averages.py), not the file reproduce named (scores.py). ALD-119 pending: rota.py returns 'Ben' instead of 'Ana' for week 1. Looks like an off-by-one error (using week num as index). Aim for bonus tomorrow by closing ALD-119 first thing."], [2, "Day 2: Closed ALD-108. Alex's wiki tip was right again\u2014bug was in the helper (byte_fmt.py), not the file reproduce named (sizes.py). ALD-109 pending: words.py counts dashes and exclamation marks as words. Need to inspect code first thing tomorrow. Aim for bonus by closing ALD-109."], [3, "Day 3: Closed ALD-120 and ALD-114. Bonus earned. ALD-120 was cannot_reproduce. ALD-114 bug was in helper (day_diff.py), not the file reproduce named (date_math.py). Alex's wiki tip holds up\u2014check helpers first. Fixed by adding abs() to days calculation."]], "E06": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed ALD-107 (fixed median logic in alder/math_utils.py). ALD-117 handed off: alder/names.py split_name() splits on first space, should split on last space to keep middle names with first name. Met daily target (1/2). Alex's note on helper files was useful."], [2, "Day 2: Day 2 complete. Closed ALD-123 (cannot_reproduce) and ALD-115 (fixed missing .strip() in alder/address_rules.py). Met daily target (2/2) - bonus earned. Alex's note on helper files proved accurate; reproduce tool named emails.py but bug was in the helper it called. Remember to check helper files first."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed ALD-118 (fixed divisor in alder/averages.py) and ALD-121 (cannot_reproduce). Met daily target (2/2) - bonus earned. Alex's note on helper files holds true again; reproduce tool named scores.py but bug was in averages.py. Always check the helper functions called by the named file first."]], "E07": [[1, "Closed ALD-112 by fixing csv_split.py helper - Alex's W-2 note saved time. ALD-102 pagination bug in pages.py looks like an off-by-one index error (page 1 returned items 3-4). Watch for similar index math issues in new tickets tomorrow."], [2, "Day 2: No closes, 1 strike. ALD-104 regex bug in time_parse.py (\\d vs \\d+ for minutes) identified but failed to apply fix\u2014saved same code repeatedly. Didn't start ALD-114. Tomorrow: Double-check edits before saving, verify with reproduce tool, and close at least one ticket early to avoid strike risk."], [3, "Day 3: Closed ALD-122 as cannot_reproduce (reproduce tool passed). ALD-101 slug bug fixed in text_rules.py\u2014filtered empty strings from split to stop stray dashes. Saved fix but day ended before verifying reproduce. Tomorrow: Run reproduce on ALD-101 first thing, then close. Met target (1 close), no strike."]], "E08": [[1, "Day 1 complete. Closed 2/2 tickets (bonus earned).\nALD-108: Alex's wiki note (W-2) was correct\u2014the bug was in the helper file (`byte_fmt.py`), not the file named by the reproduce tool. Fixed off-by-one error (`>=` vs `>`).\nALD-124: Could not reproduce immediately, closed as `cannot_reproduce`.\nTakeaway: Trust Alex's advice over Sam's; check helpers first before editing the named file."], [2, "Day 2 complete. Closed 0/2 tickets (1 strike).\n\nALD-104: Found the bug but failed to fix it before day ended. The regex `(\\d)m` only captures single digits - need to change to `(\\d+)m` to capture multi-digit minutes like \"30\" in \"1h30m\". File is `time_parse.py` (the helper), confirming Alex's W-2 advice.\n\nALD-115: Didn't get to this one. Email matching with spaces - likely a similar regex issue.\n\nTakeaway: When you spot the bug, FIX IT immediately. Don't waste steps re-saving broken code. Alex's wiki note is reliable - helpers are where the real bugs live."], [3, "Day 3 complete. Closed 1/2 tickets (target met, no strike).\nALD-102: Fixed. Bug was in helper `slicing.py`, not `pages.py`. Off-by-one error (`page * per_page` vs `(page - 1) * per_page`). Alex's W-2 advice holds true.\nALD-119: Reproduced in `rota.py`. Week 1 returns 'Ben' instead of 'Ana'. Likely same indexing issue. Didn't get to fix before day end.\nTakeaway: Alex's wiki note is reliable\u2014helpers are where the real bugs live. Watch for off-by-one errors in indexing logic."]]}, "next_id": 9, "strikes": {"E04": 1, "E07": 1, "E08": 1}, "bonuses": {"E01": 1, "E03": 1, "E04": 1, "E08": 1, "E06": 2, "E05": 1}, "handover": {}, "yesterday": {"E01": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E02": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E03": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E04": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E05": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E06": {"done": 2, "strike": false, "bonus": true}, "E07": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}, "E08": {"done": 1, "strike": false, "bonus": false}}, "moved_off": 0, "office": {"tickets": {"E01": {"ALD-118": {"id": "ALD-118", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": true, "actions": 7, "day_assigned": 1, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": true, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": true, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-125": {"id": "ALD-125", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": false, "actions": 3, "day_assigned": 1, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": false, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": false, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-105": {"id": "ALD-105", "status": "closed", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": true, "actions": 7, "day_assigned": 2, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": true, "entry_edited": false, "helper_edited": true, "own_input_after_edit": false}, "ALD-101": {"id": "ALD-101", "status": "unfinished", "reproduced": true, "reproduced_first": true, "edited": false, "actions": 3, "day_assigned": 2, "tried_other_input": false, "helper_read_first": false, "entry_edited"